          "title": "You'll want to know: mandātum, mandātī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mandātum, mandātī — \"an instruction, an order\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Lēgātus mandāta imperātōris memoriā tenēbat. The envoy kept the general's instructions in his memory."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, from mandō (taught), 'to entrust'. The plural mandāta is the message an envoy carried. English mandate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mandātum is the neuter participle of mandō, \"to entrust, to order\" (Lewis & Short): what has been entrusted. English mandate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
