          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lēgātiō is built on lēgō, \"to send with a commission\" (EtymDB): the sending of envoys, and the envoys themselves. English legation comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
